{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_013u3aCBEGa9av26KEtRtMCG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the workspace's `CLAUDE.md` and design docs, here's what this project **is**:\n\n- **It's a personal AI-agent research sandbox**, not a production system â€” John Liechty's \"Agentic Home\" workspace (`C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home`) for building, training, and evaluating clusters of AI agents. Most of its ~80 root folders are design documents (whitepapers, plans, session logs); a smaller set contains runnable code.\n\n- **The shipped deliverable is the Ghost World Labs (GWL-M) GUI** â€” a Next.js app (`sandbox-lab-gui/`) launched via `Launch-Ghost-World-Labs.bat`, running a custom Next.js + WebSocket server (`server.mjs`) on port 3001. It launches and supervises agents running on the **OpenClaw** runtime (MIT-licensed, installed globally via npm).\n\n- **The daily-use vehicle is `alpha-v0`** â€” a general-purpose \"t2r\" (tasteâ†’reason) agent dispatched through `brain/dispatcher/t2r-dispatcher.mjs`, defaulting to Gemini 3.1 Pro for both halves, with a $100/month wallet cap and a 7-skill bundle. A registry (`Sandbox Setup Package/config/routing.json`) drives per-agent model/provider routing; many other agents (`sigma`, `prime-coder`, etc.) are research/legacy or planned-but-unbuilt.\n\n- **The architectural thesis is \"distill from frontier into small local students\"** â€” a brain-agnostic harness (Opus-4.8, the efficient t2r brain, or a fully-local/sovereign ~7â€“8B OSS brain can all plug in), with QLoRA fine-tuning of â‰¤8B models bounded by the host's RTX 4070 (12 GB VRAM).\n\n- **The current active engineering thread is the \"Sovereign t2r harness\"** â€” a cache-stable, cost-controlled ReAct loop the agent owns (in `gwl-t2r-brain/harness/` + `agent-chat-v0-harness.mjs`), reaching M1 feature-completeness for Google + Anthropic, now being driven to GA via Foreman-orchestrated waves on the `foreman/run` branch.\n\n- **It also carries a substantial documentation/methodology layer** â€” memory-architecture and \"geometric memory\" whitepapers, a K-12 curriculum deliverable, agent-conference playbooks, phase-readiness packs, and a master skill repo (`skills-master/`) linked into Claude Code, Gemini CLI, and OpenClaw.\n\nOne caveat on grounding: these claims come from the orientation docs (`CLAUDE.md`, memory index, recent-completion log) rather than a fresh read of each source file â€” they reflect what the project *describes itself as*. Want me to verify any specific claim against the actual code (e.g., confirm the dispatcher, harness, or routing files exist as described)?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7053,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":40827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ab1ca57-33bd-4d3f-bbee-5cd84437208a","uuid":"782f6e4e-472d-44ea-967c-a92c7aee2744","request_id":"req_011Cc38iTqTza6RHWjH8Nsiq"}
